    "_profile_metadata": {
        "name": "Cortex L4 - Sensory Input Layer",
        "description": "Neuron model: HODGKIN_HUXLEY (dt=0.05ms). Primary sensory cortical input layer (L4): 80% excitatory spiny stellate-like neurons, 20% FS interneurons. Strongly depressing STP (U=0.6, tau_d=150ms) characteristic of thalamocortical→L4 synapses (Gil 1999). Low NMDA ratio (0.3) — thalamocortical synapses are AMPA-dominated. Symmetric STDP (A+=A-) reflecting balanced potentiation/depression for receptive field refinement. Positive OU mean current (+20pA) and high OU std (90pA) model tonic thalamic drive. Fast AMPA decay (3ms) for temporal precision.",
        "literature": [
            "Gil et al. 1999 — Thalamocortical→L4 strong depression (U≈0.6)",
            "Stratford et al. 1996 — L4 spiny stellate cell physiology",
            "Feldmeyer et al. 1999 — L4→L4 recurrent excitation",
            "Sun et al. 2006 — L4 STDP receptive field refinement",
            "Braitenberg & Schüz 1998 — L4 80:20 E/I ratio"
        ],
